    "title": "Kaukauna Police Department collects food for local pantries with 'Stuff the Squad' - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Adam Rosen No media credit provided. ,\n4 hours ago\nKAUKAUNA, Wis. (WFRV) – The Kaukauna Police Department spent time on Wednesday collecting food to help local families in need this holiday season.\nDuring their Stuff the Squad event, Kaukauna Police Officers gathered at the Piggly Wiggly to help collect food donations.\nCatching up with Local 5’s 2025 Remarkable Woman winner, Door County Candle Company’s Christiana Trapani All donated food items are set to benefit Loaves and Fishes Kaukauna Food Pantry and local affordable housing communities.\nThe most popular items varied from non-perishable foods like sauce and especially Thanksgiving food items, as the holiday approaches in just three weeks.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WFRV Local 5 - Green Bay, Appleton.",
